  "summary_en": "Segment by Connectivity splits a layer into connected regions according to a connectivity rule you choose. It outputs an integer ID per region and a mono alpha mask.",
  "inputs": [
    "source: the layer in which connectivity is detected (the only input)"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Signature: the layer type the source accepts",
    "Connectivity: Below Threshold, Above Threshold, At Threshold (neighbours on the same side of the threshold connect), At Levels (pixels in the same value band connect; band width equals Threshold)",
    "Threshold: connectivity threshold, or band width with At Levels; an eyedropper can set it",
    "Offset: with At Levels, shifts where the bands split",
    "Collapse IDs: remaps IDs to range from zero to the number of segments",
    "Outputs: id (unique integer per region, -1 for non-matching regions) and alpha (mono, 1 where the rule is met)"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "The id output can change when the resolution changes, since island shapes change the ID order",
    "Collapse IDs makes results more stable but not fully consistent; the ordering depends on each region's first pixel, so do not rely on it for animated sources",
    "Without Collapse IDs, the IDs are effectively random when the resolution changes"
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Le nœud Segment by Connectivity découpe une couche en régions connexes selon une règle de connexité, chaque région recevant un identifiant entier."
